Eh?! The beach?

104
00:03:12,844 --> 00:03:15,474
I'll go! I'll definitely go!

105
00:03:15,474 --> 00:03:17,894
There's nothing to do during summer vacation, and I'm so bored!

106
00:03:18,974 --> 00:03:21,144
Then, I'll see you next Wednesday.

107
00:03:21,144 --> 00:03:24,364
I'll contact you again once we're done sorting out the details.

108
00:03:24,774 --> 00:03:26,324
Yup, okay!

109
00:03:26,864 --> 00:03:29,944
Also, help me get Ibuki to come,

110
00:03:29,944 --> 00:03:32,784
since we're all going to the beach.

111
00:03:34,534 --> 00:03:35,914
Ah?

112
00:03:35,914 --> 00:03:36,744
Hey, Ui?

113
00:03:37,494 --> 00:03:38,874
What's wrong?

114
00:03:38,874 --> 00:03:40,084
Oh, erm...

115
00:03:40,084 --> 00:03:41,294
All right.

116
00:03:41,294 --> 00:03:43,424
Okay, I'll tell Ibuki-chan.

117
00:03:50,054 --> 00:03:54,644
Oh, Madoka-chan does volunteer work at a library during summer holidays?

118
00:03:55,144 --> 00:03:56,224
Yes.

119
00:03:56,224 --> 00:03:59,854
I read books to the children, or do picture book shows.

120
00:03:59,854 --> 00:04:03,194
She doesn't just do that, she also reads out her own works,

121
00:04:03,194 --> 00:04:05,104
which seem pretty popular with the little kids!

122
00:04:05,484 --> 00:04:06,864
Oh, I see.

123
00:04:08,194 --> 00:04:09,984
It's not all that popular...

124
00:04:10,484 --> 00:04:16,454
Well, I've enjoyed writing stories ever since I was young,

125
00:04:16,454 --> 00:04:18,534
and when I told those stories to the children,

126
00:04:18,534 --> 00:04:21,004
everyone seemed so happy, so...

127
00:04:21,374 --> 00:04:25,254
It's amazing to be able to make children happy using your own stories.

128
00:04:26,834 --> 00:04:28,214
So, are you shocked?

129
00:04:29,754 --> 00:04:31,714
It's nothing for you to boast about, is it?

130
00:04:31,714 --> 00:04:33,014
What did you say?!

131
00:04:33,014 --> 00:04:35,184
My friend's pride is my pride!

132
00:04:35,184 --> 00:04:36,394
What's wrong with boasting about it?

133
00:04:36,764 --> 00:04:40,144
By the way, Sakai-senpai, you're studying even now?

134
00:04:43,734 --> 00:04:45,984
Exam students have their battles in the summer.

135
00:04:46,444 --> 00:04:49,444
I'm sorry for having kind of forced you to come along.

136
00:04:51,284 --> 00:04:53,694
It's important to take a breather once in a while.

137
00:04:54,284 --> 00:04:55,404
And...

138
00:04:55,404 --> 00:04:57,874
What should I be sorry about?!

139
00:04:56,074 --> 00:04:57,874
This is a good chance.

140
00:04:58,164 --> 00:05:00,504
Once I'm alone together with Hoshino,

141
00:05:00,504 --> 00:05:03,334
I'll apologise properly for that incident.

142
00:05:22,144 --> 00:05:23,184
It's the sea!

143
00:05:23,184 --> 00:05:25,944
Sea, sea, sea!

144
00:05:27,604 --> 00:05:28,314
Hey!

145
00:05:28,814 --> 00:05:32,274
Do your warm-up exercises before you get into the water!

146
00:05:32,274 --> 00:05:35,864
Geez, they're so childish.

147
00:05:36,194 --> 00:05:37,364
And in comparison...

148
00:05:44,334 --> 00:05:46,834
This side is so mature.

149
00:05:46,834 --> 00:05:48,174
Y-Yeah...

150
00:05:48,174 --> 00:05:51,634
Come on, Koumoto-senpai, quickly, quickly!

151
00:05:51,634 --> 00:05:53,924
I'm not mentally prepared yet!

152
00:05:54,924 --> 00:05:57,384
Koumoto-senpai, why are you hiding?

153
00:05:57,384 --> 00:06:01,144
Your figure is good enough for you to show off!

154
00:06:01,974 --> 00:06:03,394
Ah!

155
00:06:11,024 --> 00:06:11,774
Eh?

156
00:06:12,444 --> 00:06:14,734
I didn't get thrown.

157
00:06:15,444 --> 00:06:20,704
Well, Kazuma-san was the one who invited me here...

158
00:06:20,704 --> 00:06:25,114
This, of course, shows that we're friends.

159
00:06:25,114 --> 00:06:31,584
Besides, there is no need to throw you when you touch me...

160
00:06:31,584 --> 00:06:43,474
If there's t-too much contact, I can't promise you anything...

161
00:06:44,314 --> 00:06:46,434
What do you mean, "Too much contact"?

162
00:07:04,704 --> 00:07:07,044
Madoka-chan, let me do that.

163
00:07:07,454 --> 00:07:09,874
Ah, okay...

164
00:07:23,094 --> 00:07:23,974
There you go!

165
00:07:25,304 --> 00:07:26,724
Thank you very much...

166
00:07:27,314 --> 00:07:28,974
Then, let's go!

167
00:07:28,974 --> 00:07:30,184
Okay!

168
00:07:36,734 --> 00:07:37,824
Take that!

169
00:07:38,404 --> 00:07:40,444
Take that, that, and that!

170
00:07:41,284 --> 00:07:42,664
Stop!

171
00:07:44,324 --> 00:07:46,494
Counter-attack!

172
00:07:52,464 --> 00:07:53,834
Take this!

173
00:07:53,834 --> 00:07:54,924
Eh?

174
00:07:54,924 --> 00:07:57,884
Let me engrave the power of the water gun into your memory!

175
00:08:22,744 --> 00:08:25,114
Seems like you guys are making a sand castle.

176
00:08:25,494 --> 00:08:26,704
Ah, Onii-chan.

177
00:08:26,954 --> 00:08:30,244
Ibuki, thanks for staying with Ayumu, but...

178
00:08:30,244 --> 00:08:31,794
...is it fine with you not to swim?

179
00:08:32,124 --> 00:08:33,374
Eh?!

180
00:08:33,374 --> 00:08:34,714
It's nothing much, is it?

181
00:08:34,714 --> 00:08:37,794
There's no rule stating that you have to
swim when you come to the beach, is there?

182
00:08:39,504 --> 00:08:42,384
Well, Onii-chan, Ibuki-san says she was just like me and can't-

183
00:08:42,384 --> 00:08:44,174
Ayumu-kun!

184
00:08:47,434 --> 00:08:49,264
Can't swim?

185
00:08:50,514 --> 00:08:54,814
But Ibuki, weren't you able to move along the river by emitting oil bubbles from your butt?

186
00:08:56,654 --> 00:09:01,364
There's no need to remember those kinds of details!

187
00:09:02,534 --> 00:09:07,324
Could you at least get back at me
with your fist instead of your foot...

188
00:09:08,324 --> 00:09:10,954
Being unable to swim isn't a bad thing.

189
00:09:11,544 --> 00:09:15,664
But it's good to work hard and learn to do things you couldn't before.

190
00:09:17,674 --> 00:09:20,384
Come and learn to swim with me.

191
00:09:20,384 --> 00:09:22,634
Yes, if you please!

192
00:09:23,304 --> 00:09:26,094
Then, Hinata can learn from Hoshino.

193
00:09:26,094 --> 00:09:27,304
Eh?

194
00:09:27,934 --> 00:09:29,854
I probably can't do it...

195
00:09:29,854 --> 00:09:31,064
Eh?!

196
00:09:32,354 --> 00:09:34,274
That's right. Keep it up.

197
00:09:37,194 --> 00:09:38,564
Yeah, that's the way.

198
00:09:38,564 --> 00:09:39,864
Now put your face down.

199
00:09:40,694 --> 00:09:42,614
Put my face down where?

200
00:09:43,154 --> 00:09:45,194
Well, wouldn't that be the sea?

201
00:09:45,694 --> 00:09:47,704
O-Okay.

202
00:09:52,374 --> 00:09:53,494
That's right.

203
00:09:53,494 --> 00:09:54,454
You can do it if you want to, can't you?

204
00:10:06,674 --> 00:10:08,594
Hey, are you o-

205
00:10:08,594 --> 00:10:10,974
I thought I was going to die!

206
00:10:10,974 --> 00:10:13,974
Well, you would if you held your breath for too long...

207
00:10:13,974 --> 00:10:15,684
Then say that earlier!

208
00:10:15,684 --> 00:10:17,734
I can't pull that kind of thing off!

209
00:10:17,734 --> 00:10:20,654
Also, I would be able to swim if I could pull that off!

210
00:10:22,864 --> 00:10:25,364
Ah, Ui-chan, having a break?

211
00:10:25,654 --> 00:10:29,454
I was thirsty, so I was thinking of eating some shaved ice.

212
00:10:32,074 --> 00:10:34,704
Tsumugi-san, do you know where Kazu-kun is?

213
00:10:34,704 --> 00:10:38,504
We were playing together, but he suddenly disappeared...

214
00:10:38,504 --> 00:10:41,294
If it's Kazuma-san, he's over there.

215
00:10:42,714 --> 00:10:45,674
Seems like he's teaching Ibuki-chan how to swim.

216
00:10:47,594 --> 00:10:50,434
Kazu-kun is... teaching Ibuki-chan?

217
00:10:54,764 --> 00:10:56,014
That's right, that's right!

218
00:10:56,604 --> 00:10:58,184
Keep it up!

219
00:11:03,234 --> 00:11:04,864
What's the matter, Ui-chan?

220
00:11:04,864 --> 00:11:05,734
Eh?

221
00:11:05,734 --> 00:11:07,534
I-It's nothing!

222
00:11:07,534 --> 00:11:10,614
I'll go buy some shaved ice!

223
00:11:15,034 --> 00:11:16,374
Ui-chan...

224
00:11:17,874 --> 00:11:20,004
Hoshizora e Kakaru Hashi

225
00:11:17,874 --> 00:11:20,004
Hoshizora e Kakaru Hashi

226
00:11:20,874 --> 00:11:23,004
Hoshizora e Kakaru Hashi

227
00:11:20,874 --> 00:11:23,004
Hoshizora e Kakaru Hashi

228
00:11:33,474 --> 00:11:35,904
Hey, Madoka-chan.

229
00:11:35,904 --> 00:11:37,144
Where's Tsumugi-san?

230
00:11:37,144 --> 00:11:40,854
Tsumugi-san said she had something to do and asked me to look after the belongings.

231
00:11:40,854 --> 00:11:46,064
Oh man, I even bought her some shaved ice.

232
00:11:46,064 --> 00:11:47,074
Madoka-chan, do you want this?

233
00:11:47,444 --> 00:11:47,984
Eh?

234
00:11:47,984 --> 00:11:48,944
Is it okay?

235
00:11:49,324 --> 00:11:50,404
Yup!

236
00:11:59,704 --> 00:12:01,834
Are you okay?

237
00:12:01,834 --> 00:12:03,624
It's because you ate it so quickly...

238
00:12:03,964 --> 00:12:07,884
I know, but it doesn't feel like I'm
eating shaved ice if I don't do it like this.

239
00:12:12,054 --> 00:12:13,764
Ah, that was delicious.

240
00:12:24,774 --> 00:12:28,614
I'm alone together with Nakatsugawa-senpai.

241
00:12:29,274 --> 00:12:32,574
There might not be another chance like this.

242
00:12:39,664 --> 00:12:42,294
If I want to know, I have to ask now.

243
00:12:43,084 --> 00:12:46,294
Erm, Nakatsugawa-senpai.

244
00:12:46,294 --> 00:12:47,254
What is it?

245
00:12:47,714 --> 00:12:52,924
I don't know if it's right to ask you this though...

246
00:12:53,424 --> 00:12:54,384
Go ahead.

247
00:12:57,844 --> 00:13:00,724
Then, I'll ask.

248
00:13:01,524 --> 00:13:05,194
What do you think of Kazuma-san?

249
00:13:05,604 --> 00:13:07,154
W-What do you mean?

250
00:13:07,564 --> 00:13:09,734
Well, that's...

251
00:13:11,154 --> 00:13:13,824
Whether you l-like him or not...

252
00:13:13,824 --> 00:13:14,784
Eh?!

253
00:13:14,784 --> 00:13:18,994
I don't dislike him really,

254
00:13:19,804 --> 00:13:23,164
and because I don't dislike him, I kinda like him...

255
00:13:24,124 --> 00:13:34,174
Ah, but although I do like him, this is like a love for a brother...

256
00:13:34,174 --> 00:13:36,224
Ah! That's right!

257
00:13:36,224 --> 00:13:38,844
It's the same as liking your own big brother!

258
00:13:39,434 --> 00:13:41,814
Big brother?

259
00:13:41,814 --> 00:13:45,484
Madoka-chan, why do you ask?

260
00:13:45,484 --> 00:13:47,354
That's because...!

261
00:13:47,854 --> 00:13:50,484
How should I put it...

262
00:13:50,484 --> 00:13:51,324
That's...

263
00:13:52,404 --> 00:13:53,784
